{"parentUuid":"51ed2767-e091-4fa9-8c0d-bb7edd855df8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MNNodz38pqxgFnQ12fVK5X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking about whether conflicts can occur when running multiple Claude Code sessions simultaneously. This is a valid question about Claude Code behavior.\n\nLet me think about this:\n\n1. **File conflicts**: If two sessions edit the same file simultaneously, there could be conflicts - one session's changes could overwrite the other's. There's no automatic locking mechanism.\n\n2. **Git conflicts**: If both sessions commit to the same branch, you could get merge conflicts or one session's push failing because the other already pushed.\n\n3. **Memory conflicts**: The memory system writes files to `~/.claude/projects/.../memory/`. If two sessions write to the same memory file simultaneously, there could be corruption.\n\n\n4. **Context isolation**: Each session operates independently with its own context window, so they won't be aware of each other's changes or progress.\n\n5. **Shared state**: Any shared resources like databases, running processes, or services are vulnerable - if one session modifies the database schema while another relies on the old structure, that could cause problems.\n\nThis is a legitimate question about Claude Code's multi-session behavior. Let me give a concise, accurate answer.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":141,"cache_read_input_tokens":20784,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":141},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaRXkKBSf2yyjEPMXS1xA","type":"assistant","uuid":"472b7a89-423f-428c-a98b-e3e3d02b8e3c","timestamp":"2026-04-26T01:40:43.615Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\edn_y\\renew_nineonelabs","sessionId":"e670ddef-db86-47e8-801d-40c642f32125","version":"2.1.86","gitBranch":"260414"}
{"parentUuid":"472b7a89-423f-428c-a98b-e3e3d02b8e3c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01MNNodz38pqxgFnQ12fVK5X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"좋은 질문이에요. 몇 가지 충돌 포인트가 있어요:\n\n**파일 편집**\n세션 간에 파일 잠금이 없어요. 두 세션이 같은 파일을 동시에 편집하면 나중에 저장한 쪽이 앞 쪽 변경을 덮어씌워요.\n\n**Git 상태**\n각 세션은 git 상태를 독립적으로 읽어요. 한 세션이 커밋/스테이징하면 다른 세션은 모르고 충돌하는 변경을 계속 쌓을 수 있어요.\n\n**Memory 파일**\n`MEMORY.md`나 memory 파일들을 두 세션이 동시에 쓰면 내용이 덮여쓰일 수 있어요.\n\n**컨텍스트 격리**\n각 세션은 서로의 대화를 모름. 한 세션이 \"파일 A 작업 중\"이어도 다른 세션은 그걸 알 방법이 없어요.\n\n---\n\n**실용적인 대처법:**\n- 세션마다 **담당 파일/모듈을 분리**해서 작업 (겹치지 않게)\n- 한 세션에서 커밋 후 다른 세션에서 `git pull`로 동기화\n- DB 마이그레이션이나 공유 상태 변경은 한 세션에서만\n\n어떤 식으로 세션을 나눠서 쓰고 계세요?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":141,"cache_read_input_tokens":20784,"output_tokens":746,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":141,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaRXkKBSf2yyjEPMXS1xA","type":"assistant","uuid":"48b81213-2bfb-4305-82e8-ac3364bee593","timestamp":"2026-04-26T01:40:50.043Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\Users\\edn_y\\renew_nineonelabs","sessionId":"e670ddef-db86-47e8-801d-40c642f32125","version":"2.1.86","gitBranch":"260414"}
